 "reading": [
  "On the bright-layer measure r2 raises the share from 40.5 % to 54.1 % (+13.5 points; chance 35.5 %); the gated run (--min-snr 2) gives 50.4 % and moves 38 % of the nodes.",
  "Before correction the brightest layer sits mostly 2-4 voxels outward of the ScrollFiesta surface (median +3); r2 moves the surface outward by 1.15 voxels on average (median |offset| 1.20, p90 2.35) and the median brightest position becomes +2.",
  "A model-free constant outward shift does as well or better on this measure: +1.15 voxels (r2 mean) 50.9 %, +2 voxels 55.4 %, +2.5 voxels 56.6 % vs r2 54.0 % on the same 200k-node subsample. Per node, r2 adds about 3.1 points over a constant shift of the same mean and 2.2 over each chart moved by its own median r2 offset.",
  "So most of the gain is a systematic ~1-voxel outward shift from where ScrollFiesta puts the surface (its recto: the outward dark-to-bright boundary) to the convention r2 was trained on (Paris 4 verified patches, brightest layer 0-2 voxels outward), not a per-node repair; which convention is right depends on the downstream reader.",
  "Not off-sheet: 5.7 % of nodes leave the +-2 band of the bright layer and 19.3 % enter it; 22 of 582 charts (>=100 nodes) lose 5 points or more, 426 gain 5 or more; the CT at the surface rises from 89.5 to 103.5.",
  "Core regime: nodes within 100 voxels of the axis start at 57.7 % and end at 59.4 % (median |offset| 0.75); the gain is larger farther out (300+ voxels: 39.1 -> 53.5 %). Normals pointing to the axis after orientation: 0.05 % of nodes.",
  "14335 of 98521 vertices (14.6 %) get no offset and keep their position: 2,788 belong to no face; of the rest, 91 % sit where the nearest grid node was left out as ambiguous (UV area covered by two charts or folded) and 8 % next to another chart (checked on the nearest node)."
 ],
 "verdict": "neutral: +13.5 points on the bright-layer share, but a model-free constant 2-voxel outward shift does as well (55.4 %), so the gain is mostly a convention shift, not a demonstrated repair",
